{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>According to the number of years you shall buy.</b> There is no extortion in the counting of years, as they said of blessed memory (Bava Metzi'a 56a): anything measured by measure, weight, or count, even if less than the threshold of extortion, is returnable." "<b>After the Jubilee you shall buy.</b> For it is not proper to buy during the Jubilee, so that sometimes the land will not remain in the hands of the returning owners for any time at all — and they would be as though they had never returned to their inheritance at all." "<b>Two harvests.</b> And not two of blight and mildew, as is the rule in the rental and leasing of land."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:55.952808101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}